        <definition>bool llvm::ScalarEvolution::LoopProperties::HasNoAbnormalExits</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>HasNoAbnormalExits</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::ScalarEvolution::LoopProperties::HasNoAbnormalExits</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Set to true if the loop contains no instruction that can abnormally exit the loop (i.e. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>via throwing an exception, by terminating the thread cleanly or by infinite looping in a called function). Strictly speaking, the last one is not leaving the loop, but is identical to leaving the loop for reasoning about undefined behavior. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
